\section{Sovereign Curvature Synthesis Theorem}

\begin{theorem}[\textbf{Sovereign Curvature Synthesis}]
Let $\mathcal{S}$ be the curvature synthesis operator and 
$\mathcal{C}^{A}{}_{BCD}$ the cross-domain coupling tensor. 
If each subsystem curvature tensor satisfies its own conservation law, 
then the synthesized curvature tensor satisfies:

\begin{equation}
\frac{d}{dt}
\left(
\mathcal{R}^{A}{}_{BCD}
\right)
=
0.
\end{equation}
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Since $\mathcal{S}$ preserves subsystem curvature and 
$\mathcal{C}^{A}{}_{BCD}$ preserves subsystem invariants, the 
synthesized curvature inherits conservation from each subsystem. 
Thus:

\begin{equation}
\frac{d\mathcal{R}^{A}{}_{BCD}}{dt}
=
\sum_k
\frac{d\mathcal{R}^{A}{}_{BCD}(k)}{dt}
=
0.
\end{equation}
\end{proof}

\section{Sovereign Curvature Loop}

The curvature loop is:

\begin{equation}
\mathcal{R}^{A}{}_{BCD}(t+\Delta t)
=
